# Single-page-app fallback. Read by Netlify and Cloudflare Pages; harmless
# elsewhere (it is just a file in the build output).
#
# The app now has real URLs — /shop, /about-us, /admin. Those paths exist only
# in the browser: there is no /shop/index.html on disk, so a static host asked
# for one returns 404. Every visitor arriving on a shared link, or pressing
# reload anywhere except the home page, would see the host's 404 page.
#
# 200 (not 301) so the browser keeps the requested path in the address bar —
# App.js reads it back to decide which page to open.
/*  /index.html  200
